-- title:
--   Affine Drinfeld chart at a supersingular place, q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and fix a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q$ is a non-unit, with residue field $\kappa$, and let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\ \kappa\ M'$ over $\kappa$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with geometric $j$-value in the supersingular set). Assume $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series generated by the full level-$M'$ modular function field, is contained in $F:=\mathtt{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$, the analogous base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ over $A$ with values in $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\ \kappa\ M'$ (a valuation subring with a surjective residue map onto the latter, kernel its maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and with orders and degrees of places), such that every Laurent series over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ lies in $R_0$'s integers and has residue the coefficientwise reduction of that series. Let $\pi\in A$ satisfy $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$, let $\zeta$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and let $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$, indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, and $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{ss}}$, indexed by $W$, be families of valuation subrings of $F$ subject to: $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at the line $[1:0]$ consists of the quotients $x/y$ of coefficientwise images of Laurent series over $A$ with $y$ of non-zero reduction; each $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ member is the pullback of that one along a level automorphism $\mathtt{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta\ \gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ carrying $[1:0]$ to the given line; $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective and its members are permuted by pullback along every such level automorphism (for any primitive root $\zeta'$); each $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ meets $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ exactly in $A$, is fixed by pullback along all these level automorphisms, contains an element $t$ with $t-a$ a unit for all $a\in A$, and, for $f$ in $R_0$'s integers that is non-negative at every place where $\hat\jmath$ is and whose residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, contains the image of $f$, with $f-a$ in the maximal ideal whenever $a\in A$ reduces to the value of $R_0$'s residue of $f$ at $s$. Let $K_0$ be a subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}/K_0$ algebraic and $\pi\in K_0$; let $A_0$ be a henselian discrete valuation domain with uniformiser $\varpi_0$ and an injective local homomorphism $\iota:A_0\to A$ whose image is $A\cap K_0$, inducing a surjection onto $\kappa$, with $\iota(\varpi_0)=\pi$; let $F_0\subseteq F$ be the subfield of elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, an $A_0$-algebra via $\iota$ and the constants, containing the image $\hat\jmath$ of $j$. Then for each $s\in W$ there is an $A_0$-subalgebra $B\subseteq F_0$ that is finitely generated, integrally closed in $F_0$, has $F_0$ as its field of fractions, has every non-maximal prime containing $\varpi_0B$ minimal over $\varpi_0B$, has $B_{\mathfrak p}$ a valuation subring of $F_0$ for every non-zero prime $\mathfrak p$ not containing $\varpi_0B$, contains $\hat\jmath$, is contained in $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ with $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s\cap F_0=B_{\mathfrak q_0}$ for a prime $\mathfrak q_0$ that is the unique minimal prime over $\varpi_0B$, is contained in no $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ member and in $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{ss}}_{s'}$ only for $s'=s$, is formally smooth over $A_0$, and is such that any finite set of valuation subrings $V$ of $F_0$ each properly contained in $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s\cap F_0$ and not containing $B$ has at most $q+1$ elements.
--
--   This is the $q=3$ case, at the rigid auxiliary level imposed by the prime $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the construction of the affine Drinfeld chart of the descended semistable model of the full-level modular curve at a supersingular point: a normal finitely generated $A_0$-model inside the $K_0$-rational subfield whose localisation at the unique minimal prime of the special fibre recovers the Drinfeld valuation ring attached to $s$, smooth over $A_0$, missing all Igusa rings and all other Drinfeld rings, with at most $q+1$ further valuation rings of $F_0$ below the chart. It feeds the identification of the local ring of the Drinfeld chart with that localisation in the normal model generated by $j$.
